1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,600
Every single word you speak steals three beats straight from your chest. I learned that the hard way.

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:14,868
Leo gasps, clutching his ribs as a digital counter glowing on his forearm ticks down from five hundred.

3
00:00:15,168 --> 00:00:24,456
Society adapted fast. We whisper in public. We trade sentences like gold. Whole families go mute to live past thirty.

4
00:00:24,756 --> 00:00:31,380
I never spoke a word for seven years. My counter swelled to millions. I thought I was immortal.

5
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:39,240
Then the auditor handed me the ledger. It listed every single soul tethered to my silent account.

6
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:47,820
Silence doesn't save you. It collects. Every quiet second I kept drained the heartbeat from a stranger nearby.

7
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:54,888
My neighbor's sudden cardiac arrest last month? That was me buying a year of absolute quiet.

8
00:00:55,188 --> 00:01:01,092
The less you say, the more someone else dies for your peace. We aren't saving ourselves at all.

9
00:01:01,392 --> 00:01:07,896
I open my mouth, ready to scream until my heart stops for good, to finally give it all back.

10
00:01:08,196 --> 00:01:13,524
If words cost lives, how many people died just listening to you call my name?
